batch.prompt:
Assess each object from its coordinates and answer its requested questions independently.
Observe the original image. Boxes are [left,top,right,bottom], integer thousandths of image width and height (0..999, top-left origin). Any highlight or outline in a question means the supplied box. Answer only assigned questions, using scene context as needed. Use the question's uncertainty option when evidence is insufficient. Do not decide violations. Return only JSON: regions keyed by region ID, then question ID.
{"image_size_pixels":[1536,1024],"boxes":{"r1":[377,0,831,998]},"assignments":[{"subject":"food_service_worker","questions":["face_visibility","mask_status"],"regions":["r1"]}],"questions":{"face_visibility":"Inspect the face of the person at the supplied coordinates. Use face_assessable when the nose and mouth area allows a mask assessment, including clear mask coverage. Use face_not_assessable for blur or obstruction and insufficient_visibility when the person cannot be identified.","mask_status":"Inspect the same person's face. Use wearing_mask when a mask clearly covers the nose and mouth. Use not_wearing_mask when the area is clear and no mask is worn across it. Use insufficient_visibility for an occluded, small or blurred face, or a partly worn mask."}}
